$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for N-Boc-Protected o-Aryl
Anilines. A mixture of N-Boc-protected o-bromoaniline 1 (1 equiv), the
corresponding boronic acid (1.6 equiv),
tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)-palladium (5 mol %), and potassium carbonate
(2.5 equiv) in toluene/ EtOH (4/1) (0.1 M) was stirred at 80 °C under an
argon atmosphere for 2-4 h. The reaction mixture was diluted with AcOEt,
washed with water and brine, dried over MgSO4, and concentrated under
reduced pressure. The residue was purified by column chromatography
(hexanes/AcOEt) to afford the desired product. tert-Butyl
(2-(Thiophen-3-yl)phenyl)carbamate. The product was obtained following
the general procedure (3.0 mmol scale) as a pale brown oil (586 mg, 71%)
after purification by column chromatography. Rf = 0.30 (5%
AcOEt/hexanes); 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 8.09 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.48 (dd, J =
4.9, 2.9 Hz, 1H), 7.35-7.30 (m, 2H), 7,28-7.24 (m, 1H), 7.17 (dd, J =
4.9, 1.5 Hz, 1H), 7.10-7.05 (m, 1H), 6.63 (br s, 1H), 1.49 (s, 9H); 13C
NMR (CDCl3) δ 152.8, 138.6, 135.5, 130.0, 128.4, 128.3, 126.7, 126.2,
123.4, 123.0, 119.8, 80.5, 28.3; IR (KBr) νmax 3422, 3102, 3003, 2978,
2930, 1732, 1585, 1533, 1514, 1447, 1393, 1368, 1302 cm-1; MS (FAB) m/z
275 (M+), 220 (M -t-Bu + 2H), 219 (M -t-Bu + H). Anal. Calcd for
C15H17NO2S: C, 65.43; H, 6.22; N, 5.09. Found: C, 65.24; H, 6.20; N,
5.08.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
